# Files written whole by scripts/ from catalog.json and the other root JSON
# files. GitHub collapses their diffs in pull requests and leaves them out of
# the language statistics, so a reviewer sees the row that changed rather than
# twenty regenerated files. Never edit them by hand: change the source and the
# generator, and lint.yml regenerates them (see CONTRIBUTING.md).
#
# history/*.json are the weekly refresh's snapshots (scripts/snapshot_stats.py),
# and history/daily/*.json the daily star readings (scripts/daily_stars.py),
# written whole like the rest; history/README.md is hand-written.
#
# Deliberately not listed: docs/status.md, docs/sources.md,
# docs/compatibility.md, llms.txt and site/index.html. Those are hand-written
# prose that carries generated marker blocks, and their prose is reviewed like
# any other file. The leading slash keeps examples/README.md and the package
# README, which are hand-written, out of the README patterns.
/README.md linguist-generated
/README.zh-CN.md linguist-generated
/docs/by-pattern/** linguist-generated
/docs/measured.md linguist-generated
/docs/measured.zh-CN.md linguist-generated
/docs/assets/*.svg linguist-generated
/docs/review-queue.md linguist-generated
/docs/benchmarks.md linguist-generated
/docs/benchmarks.zh-CN.md linguist-generated
/docs/zh-queue.md linguist-generated
/docs/shape.md linguist-generated
/docs/shape.zh-CN.md linguist-generated
/examples/index.json linguist-generated
/history/*.json linguist-generated
/history/daily/*.json linguist-generated
